      "url": "https://solarquarter.com/2026/11/12/cea-and-danish-energy-agency-release-technology-catalogue-to-advance-indias-energy-storage-sector/",
      "title": "India issues storage technology guide as renewable capacity expands",
      "content_html": "India’s Central Electricity Authority and the Danish Energy Agency released a catalogue on Nov. 12 to help planners and investors compare energy-storage technologies using technical and economic data adapted to Indian conditions. It covers mechanical, electrochemical, electrical and thermal systems as the country adds more solar and wind power.\n\nThe International Energy Agency forecasts nearly 4,800 gigawatts of new renewable capacity from 2026 through 2031, while about 108 gigawatts of battery storage were added worldwide in 2025, up 40% from 2024. In China, Donggao Future began production at its expanded network-storage project in Zhejiang, with a capacity of 4 gigawatt-hours, while battery-material and electrolyte projects advanced elsewhere. The catalogue is intended to guide energy planning, technology selection and investment in India.",
