      "id": "https://www.futurity.org/coffee-gut-function-changes-3352622/",
      "url": "https://www.futurity.org/coffee-gut-function-changes-3352622/",
      "title": "Danish study links regular coffee drinking to gut changes",
      "content_html": "A study of 61 healthy Danish adults found that regular coffee drinkers had more diverse gut bacteria, a lower pH in the small intestine and more contractions in the colon than people who drank coffee less often. The observational study cannot establish that coffee caused these differences.\n\nResearchers used wireless capsules to record digestive conditions in 50 participants and collected dietary records, urine tests for caffeine metabolites and stool samples. The study was published in Gut Microbiology. Transit time through the digestive tract was similar between the groups. Researchers said they do not yet know whether the lower pH in the small intestine is beneficial or harmful. They said the next step is a controlled intervention study comparing periods of coffee consumption with periods without coffee.",
