      "url": "https://www.darkreading.com/endpoint-security/n-able-n-central-offline-33-flaws",
      "title": "Remote-management provider N-able takes N-central offline, patches seven flaws",
      "content_html": "N-able, a remote-management software provider, took its hosted N-central platform offline and released a hotfix after independent researcher Sean Bales publicly disclosed 33 alleged vulnerabilities, dubbed Able2Shell. The patch addresses seven vulnerabilities. N-able also told customers with on-premises servers to keep them offline until they could safely upgrade.\n\nThe flaws could let attackers execute commands or gain administrator access. N-able said it had not confirmed exploitation, while security researchers reported internet scanning and attempts matching the published proof-of-concept exploits. N-able said it had upgraded all hosted servers and urged on-premises customers to apply the hotfix and follow its upgrade guidance before restoring normal access.",
