      "title": "Nuxalk Nation keeps support services available after fatal grizzly attack",
      "content_html": "Nuxalk Nation leaders say the grizzly attack that killed Jennifer Balcarras and her daughter, Selah Reed, near Bella Coola has renewed trauma in a community still recovering from a separate bear attack last year. The British Columbia Conservation Officer Service said forensic evidence linked a female grizzly and her three yearling cubs to the deaths. The bears were killed, and investigators believe the attack likely involved rare predatory behaviour.\n\nElected Chief Tlhmtimut Samuel Schooner said community support services would remain available for as long as needed. The Nuxalk Nation thanked conservation officers for resolving the incident, while saying the deaths had reopened trauma from the previous attack. Authorities also confirmed the four bears were not involved in that earlier attack, which injured 11 people.",
