      "url": "https://www.newscientist.com/article/2598415-re-analysis-of-black-hole-data-proves-iconic-ring-shape-really-is-there/",
      "title": "Independent analysis confirms ring in M87* black hole image",
      "content_html": "An independent reanalysis of Event Horizon Telescope observations has reproduced the bright ring surrounding the black hole's shadow in the first black hole image, confirming the central feature of the 2019 image of M87*. The study, published Nov. 11 in Nature, used a separate imaging method to address questions about whether image-processing choices had produced the ring.\n\nThe team, led by CSIRO astronomers Samuel Lai and Nithyanandan Thyagarajan, analyzed observations from 2017, 2018 and 2021. The ring in the new images had an average diameter of 42.2 microarcseconds, consistent with an estimated black hole mass of 6.5 billion solar masses. The researchers said the result supports the ring-like shape predicted by general relativity, although fine details such as ring thickness and brightness distribution still vary with the method and data quality.",
